From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dbghelp: MiniDumpWriteDump makes the callbacks Windows makes (9551)

MiniDumpWriteDump made only ThreadCallback and ModuleCallback. Windows
makes the rest, and crash reporters drive their dumps through them --
.NET's createdump hands the runtime's memory over in MemoryCallback,
Breakpad's handler uses the include callbacks and CancelCallback:

- IncludeThreadCallback for each thread and IncludeModuleCallback for
  each module before anything is written: FALSE leaves it out of the
  dump, the write flags it returns limit what is written for it;
- MemoryCallback, asked until it returns FALSE or an empty range: the
  ranges go to the memory list; RemoveMemoryCallback the same way, its
  ranges are cut out of the memory lists (a thread stack keeps its
  place; its bytes in a removed range are zeroed);
- CancelCallback, asked again for as long as it sets CheckCancel; Cancel
  fails the dump with HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(ERROR_CANCELLED) as the last
  error (a failed dump's last error is an HRESULT, as on Windows);
- IoStartCallback: when it returns S_OK every write goes to
  IoWriteAllCallback (handle, offset, buffer) instead of the file, and
  IoFinishCallback ends it;
- SecondaryFlagsCallback, IsProcessSnapshotCallback, VmStartCallback and
  WriteKernelMinidumpCallback are made with Windows' presets (no process
  snapshot handles, no virtual memory callbacks, no kernel dump);
- ReadMemoryFailureCallback when memory cannot be read; what cannot be
  read is written as zeros (it was left as a hole, and at the end of a
  file that made the dump shorter than its directory says);
- ThreadCallback is given the thread's handle;
- each callback names the process as Windows does (no process for the
  I/O and kernel-dump callbacks, the handle only for the snapshot ones).

The Wine-specific system information is written through the same path.

Gate: test/dumpcb-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit; the types and presets are the
ones Wine's own dbghelp conformance test records for Windows). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_CANCEL, SG_MUTANT_NO_IO_CALLBACK, SG_MUTANT_NO_INCLUDE_THREAD,
SG_MUTANT_NO_INCLUDE_MODULE, SG_MUTANT_NO_MEMORY_CALLBACK,
SG_MUTANT_NO_REMOVE_MEMORY (dbghelp/minidump.c).
